{"delayMs":2,"event":{"seq":3,"runId":"run_63d428319080","ts":"2026-07-14T18:44:15.888Z","type":"run.plan_generated","payload":{"plan":[{"index":0,"title":"Inspect existing repo files","detail":"Read Makefile and main.c to understand the current build structure, startup/linker setup, and any existing code before writing the driver. Confirm RTT block usage and include paths.","riskLevel":"low","hardwareAction":false},{"index":1,"title":"Write BMP180 I2C driver into main.c","detail":"Replace/augment main.c with: (1) RCC clock enable for GPIOB and I2C1; (2) GPIO alt-function config for PB8/PB9 (AF4, open-drain, no pull \u2014 BMP180 module has on-board pull-ups); (3) I2C1 init with TIMINGR=0x00310309 for ~100 kHz on 8 MHz HSI (verified against STM32CubeMX reference for F303); (4) BMP180 chip-ID read from register 0xD0 (expect 0x55); (5) read raw calibration coefficients AC1..MD (11 words from 0xAA\u20130xBF); (6) trigger one temperature + pressure measurement (OSS=0, ultra-low power), apply Bosch compensation formulas; (7) print chip-id, temperature (\u00b0C\u00d710), and pressure (Pa) via RTT SEGGER_RTT_printf loop every 1 s.","riskLevel":"low","hardwareAction":false},{"index":2,"title":"Build firmware","detail":"Run `make clean && make` via build_firmware. Confirm exit code 0 and that rtt-f303re.elf is produced.","riskLevel":"low","hardwareAction":false},{"index":3,"title":"Flash firmware to Nucleo-F303RE","detail":"Call flash_firmware (pyocd flash --target stm32f303retx rtt-f303re.elf). This is an approval-gated hardware mutation. Board is USB-powered via ST-LINK.","riskLevel":"medium","hardwareAction":true},{"index":4,"title":"Capture I2C traffic on logic analyzer","detail":"Run capture_during with I2C decode on CH0 (SDA) and CH1 (SCL) at 2 MHz sample rate for ~3 seconds while the firmware is running. Verify SCL frequency, device ACK at address 0x77, and register 0xD0 read returning 0x55.","riskLevel":"low","hardwareAction":true},{"index":5,"title":"Read RTT log","detail":"Call read_firmware_log (RTT) for ~5 seconds to capture printed chip-id, temperature, and pressure values.","riskLevel":"low","hardwareAction":true},{"index":6,"title":"Record all checks and write report","detail":"Call record_check for every registered check ID using artifacts from build, LA capture, and RTT log. Then call write_report with full evidence-linked Markdown.","riskLevel":"low","hardwareAction":false}],"riskSummary":"Hardware mutations in this run: (1) Flash \u2014 pyocd overwrites the MCU flash with the new BMP180 firmware; this is approval-gated and will pause for human sign-off before executing. (2) Logic-analyzer capture \u2014 passive tap on SDA/SCL lines, no electrical risk. The board is powered over USB through the ST-LINK; 3V3 rail is confirmed present. No erase-only or mass-erase operations are used. The only irreversible side-effect is overwriting the current flash contents, which is the intended goal. If the flash step is rejected, the run ends without touching the board."}}}
